IBM Plex Sans and Red Hat Mono, latin subsets as served by Google Fonts

Vendored rather than fetched at runtime, so that what ships is what was reviewed and the studio never
reaches out for a typeface. Both families are licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; each family's
notice sits next to its files.

  ibm-plex-sans-latin.woff2        IBM Plex Sans, variable weight 400 to 600, 45712 bytes
    source   https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/ibmplexsans/v23/zYXzKVElMYYaJe8bpLHnCwDKr932-G7dytD-Dmu1syxeKYY.woff2
    sha256   e2291e842cf5af167122a22881a740c7f2dda7716f1e8cd76680264f4a859470
    licence  ibm-plex-sans.OFL.txt

  red-hat-mono-latin.woff2         Red Hat Mono, variable weight 400 to 500, 22412 bytes
    source   https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/redhatmono/v16/jVyN7nDnA2uf2zVvFAhhzEsUWOxS.woff2
    sha256   f4bef0a36dbd4f8a34ce60ba67af24babb1334de1637c0f2680e2e18c112c2b3
    licence  red-hat-mono.OFL.txt

The files were resolved through
  https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=Red+Hat+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap
requested with a Chrome user agent, taking the latin block of each face. Google Fonts serves one file per
family for all of its weights. The notices come from https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl.

Verify a replacement before committing it:
  sha256sum *.woff2
